[interpretation]
The trace-only build differs from the failing release path by synchronous UART
prints around clock and regulator operations. Both CLDO3 and CLDO1 were really
disabled (ret=0), yet the board completed the boot. The added UART latency
therefore changes the outcome and proves a timing-sensitive MMC/PMIC power-cycle
race. This single successful boot is diagnostic evidence, not release
qualification.
